# Ablation variants are local scratch. Each tryN.py is a throwaway configuration that
# answers one question and is then worthless -- what it measured belongs in SUMMARY.md,
# which is committed. Keeping them out of history also avoids the trap unitree_rl_lab
# recorded: stale tries lingering in the tree, silently inheriting later edits to the
# configs they build on, and being re-run as if they still meant what they did.
#
# __init__.py registers whichever tryN.py happen to exist, so a checkout without any is
# fine -- it just registers no sandbox tasks.
try*.py

# ablation.py has no committed caller once the tries are ignored, so it would rot
# unnoticed -- it already had, still referencing a reset_robot_joints term that the
# production EventCfg no longer declares. Keep it local alongside the tries it serves.
ablation.py
